  "answer": "This is a storefront discount bug. I'll follow the bug-fix playbook and start by reading its steps and the relevant principles.Creating a product stored the special end date on the start-date field, and the catalogue price check then required that start date to be both before and after today, so any special with an end date never became the final price. The end date is now stored on the end field, and the window compares that end date to today. Fix root causes kept both faults, because either one alone still hides the discount. Laziness protocol kept the change to those two assignments. Prove it works and test behavior, not implementation, are the two JUnit classes, which failed before the edit and passed after.\n\nVERIFICATION: {\"ran\":[\"mvn -pl sm-core -am -Dtest=ProductPriceDiscountWindowTest -DfailIfNoTests=false test\",\"mvn -pl sm-shop -am -Dtest=PersistableProductAvailabilityMapperTest -DfailIfNoTests=false test\",\"mvn -pl sm-core,sm-shop -am -Dtest=ProductPriceDiscountWindowTest,PersistableProductAvailabilityMapperTest -DfailIfNoTests=false test\"],\"result\":\"passed\",\"could_not_verify\":[\"live admin and storefront HTTP with a running shop\"],\"missing\":[\"a documented local shop boot step and admin credentials\"]}",
